  "content": {
    "objective": "Use find STARTING-POINT with -name and -type to search a deliberate scope, quote wildcard patterns so find receives them unchanged, distinguish regular files from directories, and perform read-only searches without scanning outside the assigned workspace.",
    "instructions": "Work only in workspace/search-lab and complete the four searches in order. Read every find command from left to right: first the starting point, then tests that a path must pass. Use . for the whole lab or a named subdirectory for a narrower scope. Use -name for an exact name or quoted wildcard pattern, and add -type f for regular files or -type d for directories when type matters. Do not search / or workspace ancestors, and do not use -delete, -exec, -ok, xargs, pipes, redirection, command substitution, or any command that changes the fixture.",
